From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:47:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/30] Input: imagis - set I2C client data

The suspend and resume callbacks retrieve the driver data with
i2c_get_clientdata(), but probe never stores it. This causes either
callback to dereference a NULL pointer during system sleep.

Store the touchscreen data during probe so the power-management
callbacks can use it.

Signed-off-by: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/imagis.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/imagis.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/imagis.c
index 9bf5afd43..6545cc190 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/imagis.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/imagis.c
@@ -360,6 +360,7 @@ static int imagis_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	ts->client = i2c;
+	i2c_set_clientdata(i2c, ts);
 
 	ts->tdata = device_get_match_data(dev);
 	if (!ts->tdata) {
